The voice countdown now buzzes halfway round, the way holding the door already does. Both put a ring around the edge of the screen and fill it, but only the hold buzzed at the start, the middle and the end; the countdown buzzed at the two ends and went quiet between, so the same picture felt different depending on which screen drew it. Cancelling still works right up to the last moment, and cancelling early takes the middle buzz with it. The microphone never operates the real door.
